
%9Syntax:%9

MENTIONS%|
MENTIONS CLEAR%|

%9Parameters:%9

    CLEAR:       Clears the mentions window (/CLEAR); the log file is not
                 touched.

    Without an argument (or with any other one) switches to the mentions
    window.

%9Description:%9

    Goes to the mentions window (by default "Mentions"), where the
    mentions.pl script collects everything addressed to your nick.
    A command of the mentions.pl script.

    The window receives: channel messages and /ME actions that erssi
    marked as a hilight (your nick in the text with
    hilight_nick_matches_everywhere, or any /HILIGHT rule), all private
    messages and private /ME actions, private NOTICEs from people (not
    from servers and not sent to a channel) and DCC CHAT messages. Entries
    have the HILIGHT level, so the window gets the hilight colour in the
    window list.

    The window is created in the background at startup, has
    /WINDOW IMMORTAL on, and is recreated by the script if it gets closed.

    Every entry is also appended to mentions_log_file in the form
    "YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS [tag] place <nick> text" (mode 0600), so it
    survives a restart. A missing directory is created with mode 0700.

%9Settings:%9

    mentions_window = Mentions
        Name of the mentions window.
    mentions_log = ON
        Write mentions to the log file.
    mentions_log_file = ~/.erssi/logs/mentions.log
        The log file ('~' is your home directory).

%9Examples:%9

    /MENTIONS
    /MENTIONS CLEAR

%9See also:%9 HILIGHT, LASTLOG, WINDOW

